From e52d113e4a2e2ff052b7a2243b6dfdf24268d8e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:41:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] A message that is not one is left out, and the server
 goes on

lsp-server's stdio transport stops reading at a body that is not a
message (bad JSON, a batch array), and the server with it. The server's
own transport (stdio.rs) frames messages the same way, says such a body
in the log (window/logMessage and standard error) and reads on; headers
that cannot be read still end the connection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F8WHf8fTvjUpFp8gNQrPFQ
---
