From 331f831ec28ad977a8d3c391403a032080e8e966 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Tokens found by halving the children: opening a long file
 is linear again

rowan's token_at_offset looks at every child of each node on the way
down, and the document has one child per headline: the agenda's scan of
timestamps, which looks up the token of each, was quadratic in the
headlines (10 s to open 60 000 lines in a release build). The parser's
token_at_offset finds the same tokens by binary search on each level.

