From 37ddd63f09a3a2276403fec4160f0ea93b239a20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:58:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fixes from the end-to-end round: as Emacs does, and said
 where it does not
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Diagnostics of a changed file wait for 200 ms without a message from
  the editor: org-lint over a long file no longer runs on each keystroke
  of a burst (60 000 lines: ~0.5 s a keystroke instead of 5.5 s).
- Formatting a CRLF file: each edit stops before the line's \r.
- Citation keys completed, offered by org.cite.insert and as quick fixes
  once, when the bibliography names a file twice.
- C-c C-c on a headline's statistics cookie counts it again
  (org-update-statistics-cookies), the boxes left as they are.
- Pasting, archiving and archiving to the sibling leave the stars of
  inline tasks, as Emacs does.
- org-lint takes roam: links for links of their own type with org-roam.
- Column view asks as org-columns-edit-value: "Value: " over the allowed
  values, "Edit: " with the value; the TODO column is org.todo; not before
  the view has come.
- The agenda's changed lines: the new keyword of an entry whose parent's
  line grew, and a habit formatted again as a scheduled line.
- elisp: links are followed through Emacs after "Execute … as Elisp?";
  the types for Emacs's own programs are not completed (parity says so).
- Before an export, Emacs is told where the entries of id: links are, and
  of the roam link type.
- org.ctags.create says what ctags wrote, as shell-command does.
- protocol.org describes every request the server answers; parity.org
  the agenda's key hints left out and C-c C-c on a headline.

